ARTICLE IV: SUBSCRIPTIONS AND FINANCE

4.1 The annual subscription for Ordinary Members shall be $50.00 (Singapore dollars), payable on or before 31 January of each year.

4.2 The life membership fee shall be $500.00.

4.3 The Executive Committee may, with the approval of the AGM, revise the subscription rates from time to time.

4.4 The financial year of the Association shall commence on 1 January and end on 31 December of each year.

4.5 All moneys received by the Association shall be deposited in a bank account in the name of the Association. Cheques and other instruments of payment shall be signed by at least two of the following office-bearers: the President, the Honorary Secretary, and the Honorary Treasurer.

4.6 The Honorary Treasurer shall be responsible for keeping proper books of account, which shall be available for inspection by any member upon reasonable notice.

4.7 The accounts of the Association shall be audited annually by an independent auditor appointed at the AGM.

---

ARTICLE V: THE EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE

5.1 The governing body of the Association shall be the Executive Committee (ExCo), which shall consist of the following office-bearers:

(a) President;
(b) Vice-President;
(c) Honorary Secretary;
(d) Assistant Honorary Secretary;
(e) Honorary Treasurer;
(f) Assistant Honorary Treasurer;
(g) Six (6) Ordinary Committee Members.

5.2 All office-bearers shall be elected at the AGM by a simple majority of members present and voting, and shall hold office for a term of two years. No person shall hold the office of President for more than two consecutive terms.

5.3 The duties of the office-bearers shall be as follows:

(a) The President shall preside at all meetings of the Association and of the Executive Committee, and shall represent the Association in its dealings with external parties;

(b) The Vice-President shall assist the President and shall perform the President's duties in the latter's absence;

(c) The Honorary Secretary shall be responsible for the custody of the Association's records, the issue of notices of meetings, the keeping of minutes, and the conduct of correspondence;

(d) The Assistant Honorary Secretary shall assist the Honorary Secretary and shall perform the Secretary's duties in the latter's absence;

(e) The Honorary Treasurer shall be responsible for the collection of subscriptions, the custody of funds, and the maintenance of accounts;

(f) The Assistant Honorary Treasurer shall assist the Honorary Treasurer and shall perform the Treasurer's duties in the latter's absence;

(g) Ordinary Committee Members shall undertake such duties as may be assigned to them by the Executive Committee.

5.4 The Executive Committee shall meet at least once every month, at a time and place to be determined by the President. The SCCA Constitution specifies that the Executive Committee's meeting_cadence is monthly. Record status: current. The Honorary Secretary shall give at least seven days' notice of each meeting, together with the agenda.

5.5 A meeting of the Executive Committee shall be quorate if not less than one-third of its members, including the President or Vice-President, are present.

5.6 In the event of a vacancy arising in any office, the Executive Committee shall have the power to co-opt a member to fill the vacancy until the next AGM.

